# SRG-APP-000089-WSR-000047  -  CAT II
# The web server must generate, at a minimum, log records for system startup
# and shutdown, system access, and system authentication events.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000089-WSR-000047
group:           V-206356
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000169
control_rev5:    AU-12

contribution:    Splunk's web tier records system access in the Splunk Web HTTP access log
                 named by web.conf log.access_file and REST access in splunkd_access.log
                 for every endpoint not excluded by restmap.conf includeInAccessLog;
                 authentication successes and failures and splunkd startup and shutdown are
                 written by the product unconditionally, and the audit trail reaches a
                 searchable index when audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing is true.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.
governs:         restmap.conf - The management interface endpoints, and which clients may reach them.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           restmap.conf [<rest endpoint name>:<endpoint description string>] includeInAccessLog not_equals false
check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing not_equals false
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] log.access_file https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] log.access_file non_empty
                 reason: "log.access_file = <filename>. The HTTP access log filename. This
                         file is written in the default $SPLUNK_HOME/var/log directory.
                         Default: web_access.log" Related shipped settings:
                         log.access_maxsize = 25000000 and log.access_maxfiles = 5.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        System startup and shutdown records are written by splunkd to its own
                 service log with no configuration surface, so that part of the objective
                 is verified by inspecting the written log rather than by reading
                 configuration.
external:        The operating system's service manager decides when splunkd and Splunk Web
                 start and stop, so the boundaries of a startup and shutdown record belong
                 to it.
external:        audit.conf in Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 declares only 'queueing' under
                 [auditTrail]; the 'logging_format' key carried in the check inventory is
                 not a setting in this release's specification, so no condition is written
                 over it and the audit record format is fixed in the product.

citation:        SRG-APP-000089-WSR-000047 check text; web.conf.spec:16 ([settings]),
                 web.conf.spec:871-874 (log.access_file = <filename>, Default:
                 web_access.log); restmap.conf.spec:70 ([<rest endpoint name>:<endpoint
                 description string>]), restmap.conf.spec:138-142 (includeInAccessLog =
                 <boolean>, Default: true); audit.conf.spec:23-29 ([auditTrail], queueing =
                 <boolean>, Default: true)
finding:         Splunk Enterprise has no web access log configured, excludes REST
                 endpoints from splunkd_access.log, or sets audit.conf [auditTrail]
                 queueing to false without an input tailing the audit log, so system access
                 and authentication events are not recorded or indexed by the application.
